---

"SententiaConfig(env_file: str | None = None, cli_overrides: dict[str, Any] | None = None)":
  location: config.py
  annotations: |
    Application configuration model.
    Resolves values from ENV variables with the SENTENTIA_ prefix and from a dotenv file.
    Resolution priority: `cli_overrides` > ENV > dotenv file > built-in defaults.

    `env_file` (str | None): filesystem path to a dotenv file. When the value is None, the model uses ".env" as the default path.
    `cli_overrides` (dict[str, Any] | None): a dictionary of values provided by the CLI layer. Each key corresponds to a configuration field name. Values may be of type str, int, or bool. Non-None values take precedence over ENV and dotenv sources.

    The agent must use `pydantic` BaseModel as the base class for this model.
    The agent must apply `conventions` rules for code and test authoring.
  properties:
    "data_dir -> str": |
      Directory path containing Markdown documents for indexing. Defaults to an empty string.
    "index_path -> str | None": |
      Filesystem path to a persisted FAISS index file. None indicates an in-memory index.
    "llm_protocol -> str": |
      LLM provider identifier: "openai", "anthropic", or "ollama".
    "llm_url -> str": |
      Base URL of the LLM provider API endpoint.
    "llm_model -> str": |
      Identifier of the LLM model to invoke.
    "llm_token -> str | None": |
      API authentication key for the LLM provider. None indicates no authentication required (e.g. Ollama).
    "mcp -> bool": |
      Boolean flag that enables MCP Server mode. Defaults to False.
    "host -> str": |
      Server bind address. Defaults to "0.0.0.0".
    "port -> int": |
      Server listen port. Defaults to 8000.

